        "original_id": "9ffa89ce-b4c9-555a-8eb9-45b5b4734d7e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Columbus, Ohio\n- Products: Northland Mall, Eastland, Westland Mall, Southland\n- Concepts: Directionally-named shopping hubs, shopping malls\n\nFacts:\n- Northland Mall opened in Columbus in 1964 as an open-air shopping center and the city’s first shopping mall.\n- Eastland became one of Columbus’s directionally named shopping hubs in 1967.\n- Westland became one of Columbus’s directionally named shopping hubs in 1969.\n- Southland became one of Columbus’s directionally named shopping hubs in 1975 as a small strip center that is now closed.\n- Northland Mall was the first of Columbus’s four directionally named shopping hubs.\n- Westland Mall was an 860,000-square-foot shopping center on the west side of Columbus, Ohio, at the western intersection of U.S. Route 40 and Interstate 270.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
